Use `@Testcontainers` and `@SpringBootTest` on the test class, and annotate a container field with `@Container` (from `org.testcontainers.junit.jupiter.Container`) and `@ServiceConnection` (from `org.springframework.boot.testcontainers.service.connection.ServiceConnection`). The `@ServiceConnection` annotation creates connection details automatically for the service running in the container, taking precedence over connection-related configuration properties.

Example from the excerpts:

```java
@Testcontainers
@SpringBootTest
class MyIntegrationTests {

  @Container
  @ServiceConnection
  static Neo4jContainer neo4j = new Neo4jContainer("neo4j:5");

  @Test
  void myTest() {
    ...
  }
}
```
